{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And a great multitude of cattle.</b> Because they were exceedingly wealthy, they cherished their wealth, and on account of cherishing their wealth they separated from their brothers and settled outside the land of Israel. Therefore they were exiled before all the tribes, as it is said: ״ויגלם לראובני ולגדי ולחצי שבט המנשי״, and as it is written: ״כי לא ממוצא וממערב ולא ממדבר הרים כי אלהים שופט זה ישפיל וזה ירים״ — meaning: whatever a person labors for and goes out in trade, traveling from east to west and pressing the moment to grow rich — he does not become wealthy because of this. And even if he goes through wildernesses and to the mountains — what is ״ולא ממדבר הרים״? Rabbi Abba said: every 'mountains' in Scripture are actual mountains, except for this one, which is an expression of raising up — meaning that a person is not elevated through this. ״כי אלהים שופט זה ישפיל וזה ירים״ — He takes possessions from this one and gives them to that one. And why are they called נכסים? Because they are נכסין from this one and revealed to that one. And why are they called זוזים? Because they זזין from this one and go to that one. And why are they called ממון? — meaning: why do you count them? And why are they called מעות? — they hear (משמעותין) the law. And Rabbi Abba further said: Hannah said: ״ה' מוריש ומעשיר משפיל אף מרומם״ — meaning: through the anger that He brings upon this one, that one is raised up. So too you find with the children of Gad and the children of Reuben — what is written above? ״אנשי הצבא בזזו איש לו״ — through the anger that the Holy One, blessed be He, brought upon Midian, the children of Gad and the children of Reuben grew rich. And likewise through the anger that the Holy One, blessed be He, brought upon Egypt, Israel grew rich. And so our Sages of blessed memory said: Three gifts did the Holy One, blessed be He, place in His world: wisdom, strength, and wealth. One who merits one of them merits all of them — and when? When they come through the wisdom of Torah and fear of HaShem; but otherwise, strength and wealth do not avail a person at all. And thus Jeremiah said: ״אל יתהלל חכם בחכמתו ואל יתהלל הגבור בגבורתו כי אם בזאת יתהלל המתהלל״ etc. And I too heard about this what our Sages of blessed memory said in tractate Niddah, chapter כל היד: that one angel is appointed over pregnancy, and his name is Laylah, and he brings the drop before the Holy One, blessed be He, and says: this drop — what will become of it? Wise or foolish, strong or weak, poor or rich — but wicked or righteous he does not say, for that depends on the person's own will, as we say: everything is in the hands of Heaven except fear of Heaven. And this is what the verse says: ״אל יתהלל חכם בחכמתו״ — for it has been decreed upon him from the day he was formed; ״כי אם בזאת יתהלל המתהלל השכל וידוע אותי״ — for this was not decreed upon him, for this is in his hands. And these three — when they are not from the Holy One, blessed be He, their end is to be taken from him. And so our Sages of blessed memory taught: two wise men were there and were wealthy — they arose in the world: one from Israel and one from the nations of the world: Korah and Haman, and both were lost from the world. And so our Sages of blessed memory said: ״עושר שמור לבעליו לרעתו״ — this is the wealth of Korah and of Haman. And all this, why? Because their gift was not from the Holy One, blessed be He, but they snatched it for themselves."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:39.769824257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}